WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.680
In January 2022, a dozen eggs in the US

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:07.090
cost about 1.93 dollars on average.

3
00:00:07.090 --> 00:00:10.030
A year later: 4.82.

4
00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:14.930
By March 2025, a record 6.23 dollars.

5
00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:19.790
Bird flu outbreaks had forced producers
to cull millions of egg-laying hens.

6
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.820
Then, as flocks were rebuilt,

7
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.380
the price fell back.

8
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.850
So when a harvest fails or buyers rush in,

9
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.620
which way do prices move,

10
00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:29.910
and how far?

11
00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:33.010
In this mission, you'll shift
supply and demand in a graph

12
00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.770
lab and track the new
equilibrium price and quantity.

13
00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:39.180
Then you'll see why
egg prices had to climb

14
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.780
so far before the market cleared.

15
00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:44.740
Your mission: predict
which way prices move,

16
00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:45.790
and how far.
